971 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Trading is like being a smart shopper and seller in the world of stocks. Imagine you're at a big marketplace where, instead of toys or clothes, people buy and sell tiny pieces of companies called stocks. Your goal as a trader is to buy these stocks when their prices are low and sell them when the prices go up. It's similar to how you might buy a rare trading card when it's not popular, wait for it to become valuable, and then sell it for more than you paid.)
/E (Trading is like being a smart shopper and seller in the world of stocks. Imagine you're at a big marketplace where, instead of toys or clothes, people buy and sell tiny pieces of companies called stocks. Your goal as a trader is to buy these stocks when their prices are low and sell them when the prices go up. It's similar to how you might buy a rare trading card when it's not popular, wait for it to become valuable, and then sell it for more than you paid.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
972 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In the stock market, you're dealing with real companies like Apple, Google, or Tesla. When you buy a stock, you own a tiny part of that company. The price of these stocks goes up and down all day long, based on how well the company is doing and what people think about it. As a trader, your job is to guess when a stock price will go up or down and make smart choices about when to buy or sell.)
/E (In the stock market, you're dealing with real companies like Apple, Google, or Tesla. When you buy a stock, you own a tiny part of that company. The price of these stocks goes up and down all day long, based on how well the company is doing and what people think about it. As a trader, your job is to guess when a stock price will go up or down and make smart choices about when to buy or sell.)
