/ActualText (Robinhood: For beginners, Robinhood can be a great starting point. Its user-friendly interface makes it easy to explore and understand key concepts like strike prices, expiration dates, and price movements. It's an excellent platform for getting comfortable with the basics of trading. The simplicity of Robinhood's app can help new traders focus on learning fundamental concepts without being overwhelmed by complex features. It's particularly useful for getting a feel for how the market movements can affect your trade. However, it's important to note that Robinhood has faced criticism for certain practices, particularly during high-volatility events like the GME/AMC short squeeze. Their customer support can also be slow at times. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
