1239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (IV Crush occurs when high implied volatility \(IV\) rapidly decreases, causing the value of your options to decline significantly, similar to how a balloon deflates quickly when the air is let out.. Here's the kicker - your option can lose value even if the stock moves in your favor. It's like winning the race but finding out the prize money got cut.)
/E (IV Crush occurs when high implied volatility \(IV\) rapidly decreases, causing the value of your options to decline significantly, similar to how a balloon deflates quickly when the air is let out.. Here's the kicker - your option can lose value even if the stock moves in your favor. It's like winning the race but finding out the prize money got cut.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (When Does This Happen? IV Crush occurs because implied volatility represents the market's expectations of how much the price of an underlying asset will move in the future. When a big event is on the horizon, such as an earnings report or major news announcement, uncertainty is high, and so is implied volatility. Traders are willing to pay a premium for options because they expect significant price movement, either up or down.)
/E (When Does This Happen? IV Crush occurs because implied volatility represents the market's expectations of how much the price of an underlying asset will move in the future. When a big event is on the horizon, such as an earnings report or major news announcement, uncertainty is high, and so is implied volatility. Traders are willing to pay a premium for options because they expect significant price movement, either up or down.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (However, once the event passes, the uncertainty disappears, and the actual movement in the stock price is often less dramatic than expected. As a result, the implied volatility drops sharply, which is known as IV Crush. This sudden decrease in IV causes the time value portion of the option's price to decline, regardless of whether the stock moved in the direction you anticipated.)
/E (However, once the event passes, the uncertainty disappears, and the actual movement in the stock price is often less dramatic than expected. As a result, the implied volatility drops sharply, which is known as IV Crush. This sudden decrease in IV causes the time value portion of the option's price to decline, regardless of whether the stock moved in the direction you anticipated.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
