1365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Understanding the bid/ask spread is crucial for options trading. While it's generally wise to aim for the best price, the nature of breakout trading often requires quick action. When dealing with high-volume, big tech stocks, the tight spreads usually mean the benefits of immediate execution outweigh the small cost of buying at the ask price. Remember, in fast-moving markets, a few cents saved could mean dollars lost in missed opportunities. Always consider your strategy, the stock's liquidity, and the potential move when deciding how to place your order. Ultimately, successful trading is about balancing cost-efficiency with timely execution to maximize your profit potential.)
