1408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In the stock market, volume is one of the most important indicators of market activity and sentiment. It represents the total number of shares traded during a specific time period and can provide valuable insights into the strength and direction of a market move. To better understand the role of volume, think of the stock market as a massive auction house where buyers and sellers come together to exchange shares. Volume is essentially the count of how many "items" \(in this case, shares\) changed hands during a specific period, much like measuring the foot traffic in a store. The more people \(buyers and sellers\) participating, the higher the volume.)
/E (In the stock market, volume is one of the most important indicators of market activity and sentiment. It represents the total number of shares traded during a specific time period and can provide valuable insights into the strength and direction of a market move. To better understand the role of volume, think of the stock market as a massive auction house where buyers and sellers come together to exchange shares. Volume is essentially the count of how many "items" \(in this case, shares\) changed hands during a specific period, much like measuring the foot traffic in a store. The more people \(buyers and sellers\) participating, the higher the volume.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [8]
>>
