1425 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3573 0 R
/ActualText (Volume Spikes: Significant spikes in volume can often precede or coincide with reversals in market direction. For instance, after a prolonged downtrend, a sudden large increase in volume during a price rally might indicate that buyers are stepping in, possibly marking the end of the downtrend.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
1426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Climax Volume: Sometimes, a trend will end with a period of "climax volume," where there is a sudden surge in trading activity. In an uptrend, this might occur when the last of the buyers have entered the market, leaving fewer buyers to sustain the trend. Similarly, in a downtrend, climax volume might occur when sellers have exhausted themselves, leading to a reversal.)
/E (Climax Volume: Sometimes, a trend will end with a period of "climax volume," where there is a sudden surge in trading activity. In an uptrend, this might occur when the last of the buyers have entered the market, leaving fewer buyers to sustain the trend. Similarly, in a downtrend, climax volume might occur when sellers have exhausted themselves, leading to a reversal.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
