/T (    4. Divergence Between Price and Volume)
/E (    4. Divergence Between Price and Volume)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3576 0 R
/ActualText (What is Divergence?: Divergence between price and volume can be a key signal of a potential change in trend. For example, if the price is making new highs but the volume is decreasing, this is known as bearish divergence and might indicate that the uptrend is running out of steam.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1437 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3577 0 R
/ActualText (Bullish Divergence: On the other hand, if the price is making new lows but volume is decreasing or flat, it might signal that the downtrend is losing strength, potentially leading to a reversal or a bounce.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
