/Pg 44 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3580 0 R
/ActualText (The Role of Volume in Trends: Volume is a key indicator that confirms the strength and sustainability of a market trend. When the volume increases in the direction of the trend, it signals that the trend is supported by a growing number of participants, which adds momentum and makes it more likely to continue.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3581 0 R
/ActualText (Analogy: Think of a snowball rolling downhill. As it rolls, it gathers more snow \(volume\), increasing in size and speed. Similarly, a trend that is accompanied by rising volume is likely to gain momentum and strength, making it more reliable.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3582 0 R
/ActualText (Practical Example: If a stock is in an uptrend and you notice that each upward price movement is accompanied by higher volume, it confirms that buyers are actively pushing the price higher. This makes the uptrend more trustworthy.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 792 0 R
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [8]
>>
