>>
endobj
1454 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Volume as an Early Warning: Just as increasing volume confirms a trend, decreasing volume can signal a weakening trend. When a trend continues but the volume starts to diminish, it might indicate that the trend is running out of steam, and a reversal could be on the horizon. Analogy: Imagine a car running out of gas. It might keep moving for a short distance due to momentum, but eventually, it will slow down and stop. Similarly, a trend with declining volume may keep going for a bit, but the lack of fuel \(volume\) suggests that it could soon reverse.)
/E (Volume as an Early Warning: Just as increasing volume confirms a trend, decreasing volume can signal a weakening trend. When a trend continues but the volume starts to diminish, it might indicate that the trend is running out of steam, and a reversal could be on the horizon. Analogy: Imagine a car running out of gas. It might keep moving for a short distance due to momentum, but eventually, it will slow down and stop. Similarly, a trend with declining volume may keep going for a bit, but the lack of fuel \(volume\) suggests that it could soon reverse.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
