1473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3587 0 R
/ActualText (Institutional Activity Clues: Volume can also provide insights into accumulation \(buying\) or distribution \(selling\) by large institutional players. When you see large volume on relatively small price movements, it might indicate that big players are quietly building or reducing their positions.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3588 0 R
/ActualText <>
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1475 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3589 0 R
/ActualText (Practical Example: If a stock is trading within a tight range but you observe unusually high volume, it could suggest that institutions are accumulating shares before a significant move. Conversely, high volume during a small price decline might indicate distribution before a larger sell-off.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1476 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (5. Practical Application)
/E (5. Practical Application)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1477 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3590 0 R
/ActualText (Understanding Volume in Action: Volume analysis becomes most powerful when applied in real-time trading. For instance, during an uptrend, you might notice green \(buying\) volume bars increasing in both frequency and size. This suggests that more and more traders are participating in the uptrend, indicating strong support for the price movement and increasing the likelihood that the trend will continue.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
