1483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3591 0 R
/ActualText (Compare Current Volume to Average Volume: Unusually high or low volume relative to the average can often precede significant price moves. For example, a sudden spike in volume after a period of low volume could indicate the start of a new trend.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3592 0 R
/ActualText (Look for Volume Divergences: If the price is making new highs but the volume is decreasing, it might signal that the trend is weakening and a reversal could be imminent. Conversely, if the price is making new lows but the volume is decreasing, the downtrend might be losing strength.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3593 0 R
/ActualText (Use Volume in Conjunction with Price Action: A large price move on low volume might not be as significant as a smaller move on high volume. High volume validates price moves, confirming that they are backed by market participation and not just a few traders.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
