/P 796 0 R
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3597 0 R
/ActualText (Fear and Greed: As price approaches a support level, buyers step in due to the fear of missing out on a good deal. At resistance, sellers become active due to greed and the desire to take profits.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3598 0 R
/ActualText (Institutional Influence: Large institutions often place significant orders at certain levels. These large volume orders can create support or resistance as they're gradually filled.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3599 0 R
/ActualText (Technical Indicator Confluence: When multiple technical indicators suggest a level is significant, it can become a self-fulfilling prophecy as more traders watch and act on these levels.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3600 0 R
/ActualText (Herd Mentality: As more traders recognize and act on support and resistance levels, their significance increases. This herd behavior reinforces the power of these levels.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Understanding this psychology allows you to anticipate market behavior more accurately. However, remember that while these psychological factors often influence price action, they aren't guarantees. Markets can and do break through significant levels, especially when fundamental factors change.)
/E (Understanding this psychology allows you to anticipate market behavior more accurately. However, remember that while these psychological factors often influence price action, they aren't guarantees. Markets can and do break through significant levels, especially when fundamental factors change.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
