/T (Definition: A falling wedge is a bullish pattern that can either indicate a reversal during a downtrend or act as a continuation pattern during an uptrend. It signals that the current downtrend or consolidation phase may be losing momentum, with a potential breakout to the upside expected. Think of it as a coiled spring that's been compressed and is ready to bounce back up.)
/E (Definition: A falling wedge is a bullish pattern that can either indicate a reversal during a downtrend or act as a continuation pattern during an uptrend. It signals that the current downtrend or consolidation phase may be losing momentum, with a potential breakout to the upside expected. Think of it as a coiled spring that's been compressed and is ready to bounce back up.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [10]
>>
