1594 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3624 0 R
/ActualText (Body: The thick part of the candlestick is called the body. It shows the range between the open and close prices. If the close is higher than the open, the body is usually filled or colored \(often green or white\), indicating a bullish \(upward\) movement. Conversely, if the close is lower than the open, the body is usually hollow or colored differently \(often red or black\), indicating a bearish \(downward\) movement.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
