<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (These quick reversals can be particularly deceptive because they initially give the impression of a breakout, encouraging traders to enter positions. However, the rapid return of the price to its previous range is a clear signal that the breakout is not genuine. Observing the speed and decisiveness of the reversal can help you determine whether a breakout is likely to hold or fail.)
/E (These quick reversals can be particularly deceptive because they initially give the impression of a breakout, encouraging traders to enter positions. However, the rapid return of the price to its previous range is a clear signal that the breakout is not genuine. Observing the speed and decisiveness of the reversal can help you determine whether a breakout is likely to hold or fail.)
