1722 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Failure to Hold: In a genuine breakout, the price typically breaks through a key level and then holds above \(in the case of a resistance breakout\) or below \(in the case of a support breakout\) that level. However, in a fakeout, the price may initially breach the level but then struggles to maintain its new position.)
/E (Failure to Hold: In a genuine breakout, the price typically breaks through a key level and then holds above \(in the case of a resistance breakout\) or below \(in the case of a support breakout\) that level. However, in a fakeout, the price may initially breach the level but then struggles to maintain its new position.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [6]
>>
