/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The market is ever-changing, and successful traders are those who can adapt their strategies to these changes. Rigid expectations of how the market "should" behave will only lead to frustration and losses. Mental flexibility involves being prepared to adjust your approach based on what the market is actually presenting, not what you hope it will do. This adaptability is a cornerstone of risk acceptance, as it allows you to pivot when necessary and avoid stubbornly sticking to a losing strategy.)
