2383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Acknowledge the Worst-Case Scenario Before entering any trade, mentally accept the maximum possible loss. Calculate and be prepared for the worst outcome of every position you take. This mental preparation helps reduce the emotional impact of losses when they occur and keeps you grounded in reality. Focus on Process, Not Outcome Concentrate on executing your trading strategy correctly, rather than focusing solely on making money. Success in trading is not just about profitability; it's about consistently following a well-thought-out plan. Evaluate your trades based on how well you adhered to your strategy, not just on the financial outcome. Develop a Comprehensive Risk Management Plan A solid risk management plan is the backbone of any successful trading strategy. Set clear stop-losses and define appropriate position sizes relative to your account. Never enter a trade without a predetermined exit strategy for both profit and loss scenarios. Regularly review and adjust your risk management approach as your account grows or as market conditions change. This proactive approach ensures that you're always prepared for the inherent risks of trading.)
/E (Acknowledge the Worst-Case Scenario Before entering any trade, mentally accept the maximum possible loss. Calculate and be prepared for the worst outcome of every position you take. This mental preparation helps reduce the emotional impact of losses when they occur and keeps you grounded in reality. Focus on Process, Not Outcome Concentrate on executing your trading strategy correctly, rather than focusing solely on making money. Success in trading is not just about profitability; it's about consistently following a well-thought-out plan. Evaluate your trades based on how well you adhered to your strategy, not just on the financial outcome. Develop a Comprehensive Risk Management Plan A solid risk management plan is the backbone of any successful trading strategy. Set clear stop-losses and define appropriate position sizes relative to your account. Never enter a trade without a predetermined exit strategy for both profit and loss scenarios. Regularly review and adjust your risk management approach as your account grows or as market conditions change. This proactive approach ensures that you're always prepared for the inherent risks of trading.)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [9]
