/S /H2
/T (Avoiding Emotional Spillover One of the biggest challenges in trading is preventing previous trades from dictating your current decision-making process. It's easy to become overconfident after a series of wins or overly cautious after a string of losses. However, each trade should be evaluated on its own merits, independent of what happened before. Emotional spillover can cloud your judgment, leading to impulsive decisions that deviate from your trading plan.)
