/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Consistency is key to overcoming the subjective nature of perception in trading. Sticking to your trading plan regardless of recent outcomes helps ensure that your decisions are based on logic and strategy rather than on emotional impulses. By evaluating setups based on predefined criteria, you reduce the likelihood of making decisions that are influenced by temporary psychological states or cognitive biases.)
/E (Consistency is key to overcoming the subjective nature of perception in trading. Sticking to your trading plan regardless of recent outcomes helps ensure that your decisions are based on logic and strategy rather than on emotional impulses. By evaluating setups based on predefined criteria, you reduce the likelihood of making decisions that are influenced by temporary psychological states or cognitive biases.)
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [5]
