/T (Regular Self-Assessment Keeping a trading journal is an effective way to track your perceptions and decisions. In this journal, record not only the details of your trades but also your thoughts, emotions, and reasoning at the time of each trade. Periodically review your journal to identify patterns in your thinking that may indicate biases or emotional influences. This self-assessment can help you refine your approach and improve your decision-making over time.)
