/T (Discipline in trading means resisting the urge to deviate from your strategy, even when the market presents tempting opportunities that fall outside of your plan. This temptation might come in the form of a sudden price spike, a hot tip, or a gut feeling. However, deviating from your plan can lead to inconsistent results and increased risk. By sticking to your trading rules, you create a consistent approach that helps you weather the inevitable ups and downs of the market.)
