2618 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Panic Selling When the market becomes turbulent, fear can trigger panic selling. This is when you close positions at a loss out of fear that the market will continue to move against you. Panic selling often happens during sharp market downturns or unexpected news events, where emotions override rational analysis, leading to hasty decisions that may not be in your best interest.)
/E (Panic Selling When the market becomes turbulent, fear can trigger panic selling. This is when you close positions at a loss out of fear that the market will continue to move against you. Panic selling often happens during sharp market downturns or unexpected news events, where emotions override rational analysis, leading to hasty decisions that may not be in your best interest.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
2619 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (HODL'ing \(Holding On for Dear Life\) Conversely, fear can also lead to holding onto losing positions for too long, hoping for a turnaround. This behavior is rooted in the fear of realizing a loss, which can cause you to ignore signs that the market is unlikely to recover. By clinging to a losing trade, you might incur even greater losses, exacerbating the situation.)
/E (HODL'ing \(Holding On for Dear Life\) Conversely, fear can also lead to holding onto losing positions for too long, hoping for a turnaround. This behavior is rooted in the fear of realizing a loss, which can cause you to ignore signs that the market is unlikely to recover. By clinging to a losing trade, you might incur even greater losses, exacerbating the situation.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [8]
